{{also|Tauchen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|tūchen}}, {{m|gmh|touchen}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh||-tūhhan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*dūkaną}}. Cognate to {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|de|duiken}}. The word had become obsolete in [[Upper German]], but was later reintroduced on the basis of [[Central German]] {{m|gmh||dūchen, tūchen}} and {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|dūken}}, which had remained common. In the course of this process, the originally strong verb became weak. A derivative with [[Low German]] consonantism is {{m|de|ducken}} (cognate to and synonymous with {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|duck}}).

